{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1790266149,"nonce":"OQTTK0unB8/aSHTwooKU7gkmGH8=","message":"**Handoff: paused mid-round (2026-09-24). Covers d7d9c57 and 50df87a.**\n\n**Where it is**\n- Branch `spec/d7d9c57-new-game-load`, worktree `/home/dorian/projects/rimworld/autorimmer/.claude/worktrees/agent-a3a6972645eebe8db`.\n- Last commit `6cdf858` (wip). Before it: `e4cd85c` (load), `8b76d70` (drain). Base `769fdd5`. Nothing merged or pushed, and no DLL committed.\n- The tree builds: `dotnet build -c Release`, 0 warnings, 0 errors. `rwa/selftest.sh` passes 278/0 as of `e4cd85c`. It must be run from the repo root.\n- Nothing has been run in front of a game.\n\n**Done**\n- `8b76d70`, the menu-live drain. It is `RootDrain.cs`, a Harmony postfix on `Verse/Root.Update`. It runs every frame in both scenes, after `LongEventsUpdate` and before the Play scene's `Game.UpdatePlay`. It executes commands only when no long event is running and `Root.destroyed` is false.\n  - A verb opts in with `[Verb(..., MenuCapable = true)]`. Verbs without the flag are routed byte-identically to before.\n  - The drain has its own `Runtime.RootBeat`. `Runtime.Heartbeat` and `gameLoaded` are unchanged.\n  - `status.json` and the `status` verb gain `phase` (playing|switching|loading|menu). It is absent while the drain is not live.\n  - `rwa` still has five verdicts. It grades a live main thread with no game as `menu` rather than `stalled`, including back at the menu after a game.\n- `e4cd85c`, `load {name, load_anyway?}` (`LifecycleVerbs.cs`) plus the driver `GameSwitch.cs`.\n  - It refuses before anything unloads:\n    - a stray key;\n    - an invalid or unknown name (the refusal lists the saves);\n    - permadeath;\n    - `busy`;\n    - a failed `PreLoadUtility` mod or version check unless `load_anyway:true`.\n  - The load is `GameDataSaveLoader.LoadGame`, queued as a synchronous long event, never run inside `UpdatePlay`.\n  - The boundary is the existing `LoadedGame` -\u003e `GameBoundary` reset. Its `session` row is now `by:\"agent\"` with the command id.\n  - The game is paused through `ExecuteWhenFinished`, the point where `Prefs.PauseOnLoad` pauses.\n  - The result is written on the new game's first `GameComponentUpdate`. It carries `tick`, the unchanged `sid`, `session_seq`, `journal_seq` and the autostart report.\n  - A switch stranded at the menu is answered `load-failed` by the root drain.\n  - `MenuCapable` verbs route by the drain's phase. A second switch is `busy` at once.\n  - `rwa` gives `load` a 600 s bound.\n- `6cdf858` (wip), `new-game {scenario, storyteller, difficulty, seed?, discard_unsaved?}`. It is the main menu's \"Dev quick test\" events (`SetupForQuickTestPlay` + `PageUtility.InitGameStart`) with the four choices substituted. From a running colony, `GenScene.GoToMainMenu` runs first, in the same kickoff event.\n  - Gates:\n    - `showInUI` scenarios;\n    - `listVisible` storytellers;\n    - any difficulty (custom copies Rough);\n    - `discard_unsaved` for the ConfirmQuit dialog;\n    - permadeath is refused.\n  - The result reads back the scenario, storyteller, difficulty and seed, and publishes `scenario.parts`.\n\n**Not done**\n- Self-review of `6cdf858`.\n- `rwa`: add `new-game` to `SWITCH_OPS`, and mention `rwa new-game` in the `menu` advice.\n- Docs:\n  - `rwa/README.md` (the two verbs, `phase`/`switch`, the `menu` meaning, the timeouts);\n  - `JOURNAL.md` (the `session` row's `by` for a switch, and the `action` rows `load`/`new-game` with `requested`/`failed`);\n  - a `DESIGN.md` decisions-log entry for the drain and the resolutions below.\n- `accept/d7d9c57-new-game-load.md`, the numbered `rwa` command list. It must include the autostart case.\n- The resolutions still have to be posted as comments on both issues.\n- Final report.\n\n**Next steps**\n1. Review `6cdf858`, then build.\n2. Make the `rwa` changes and run the self-test from the repo root